course: dictionary
lesson: 14551
title: The word petty
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Petty is an adjective, so it describes a noun. It can mean small and unimportant: «They argued about petty problems, like who had the blue pen.» The problems are tiny, so petty means small.
explain: Petty can also mean caring too much about small things in a mean way. «Don't be so petty!» means stop making a fuss about something tiny. The clue is the feeling: the speaker thinks the other person is being mean about nothing.
explain: Petty can describe small crimes and small amounts of money too. «He was caught for petty theft after taking two sweets» means he stole something small. Petty cash is a small amount of money kept for small costs.
fact: Petty is an adjective. Its forms are petty, pettier and pettiest.
fact: «Petty» means small and unimportant.
fact: «Petty» can also mean caring too much about small things in a mean way.
fact: «Petty theft» means stealing small things.
fact: «Petty cash» is a small amount of money kept for small costs.
exercise: «The argument was about petty problems, like who had the last biscuit.» What does petty mean here? | Very dangerous | Loud and angry | Brand new | *Small and unimportant
exercise: «Don't be so petty!» What does the speaker mean? | Let's go out and play | Please be more careful with your money | *Stop making a fuss about something tiny | You are very tall
exercise: Which phrase means a small amount of money kept for small costs? | Petty theft | *Petty cash | Petty grandad | Petty kings
test: The shop had a box of petty cash for small costs like pens and paper. What is petty cash? | Money for big bills | *A small amount of money kept for small costs | A kind of cake | A gift for a friend
test: «He was caught for petty theft after taking two sweets.» What does petty theft mean? | Giving money away | Stealing a car | *Stealing small things | Lending a book
exam: In «Don't be so petty about who won the game», what does petty mean? | *Caring too much about small things in a mean way | Lost | Happy and proud | Very tall
